[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mHow should the refresh gap be resolved (ID survives refresh, in-memory token does not)?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mClear ID if no token (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mOn load, a stored user ID with no live token is treated as logged-out and cleared. Purely client-side, no backend [39m
     [38;5;246mdependency, never shows a half-authenticated state.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m HttpOnly cookie from backend
     [38;5;246mBackend sets the session cookie so login genuinely survives refresh. Best user experience, but depends on backend [39m
     [38;5;246mwork and needs a CSRF story.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Design the seam, decide later
     [38;5;246mBuild an isLoggedIn() check now with the clear-on-missing-token behavior, documented as provisional pending the [39m
